  }
 ],
 "synopsis": "Ratnadeep Retail Limited has received SEBI approval to raise funds through an initial public offering. The proposed IPO features a fresh issue of equity shares worth up to Rs 400 crore, alongside an offer for sale of up to 1.49 crore shares by promoter selling shareholders. The Hyderabad-based retailer plans to use Rs 40 crore of the fresh issue proceeds for debt repayment and Rs 260 crore to open new stores under Ratnadeep and National Mart formats, with the remainder allocated for general corporate purposes. The company filed its draft red herring prospectus in July 2026 and operates supermarkets, premium food stores, and hypermarkets across Telangana, Andhra Pradesh, and Karnataka.",
